  "raw_text": "288\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nth\n-\nintro\n):\n \nYas upla ba kaikbia Jehova wina lan\n \ntakisa, man wina apia.\n \n–\n \nCause the person to look to learn from\n\nJehovah, not from you.\n \n/ Haga que la persona busque aprender de Jehová, no de usted.\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nth\n-\n3\n):\n \nYas upla ba kau lan takan daukbia.\n \n–\n \nCause the person to desire to learn more.\n \n/ Hacer que la persona desee\n\naprender más.\n)\n\nYayabra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \ngiver, person who gives\n \n/ dador, persona que da\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlv33\n):\n \nJehova sika wan Papaskra bara wan Rayaka Yayabra sa\n \n–\n \nJehovah is our Creator and Life\n-\nGiver\n \n/ Jehová es\n\nnuestro creador y\n \ndador de vida\n)\n\nCher yayabra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nattendant\n \n/ acomodador\n\nYabal\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nroad, way, street, path\n \n/ camino, calle\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 2:3\n):\n \nAi yabalka nani ra wapbia\n \n–\n \nto walk in his ways\n \n/ caminar en sus caminos)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Param Marikan 15:3\n):\n \nyabalkam nani ba wapni ... sa\n \n–\n \nyour ways are righteous\n \n/ tus caminos son justos)\n\nKasak lâka yabalka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nway of truth\n \n/ camino de la verdad\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb100\n):\n \nTimoti kasak lâka yabalka ra ban wapaia bara nahki smalkaia ba lan mai daukbia\n \n–\n \nTimothy will teach you\nto continue to walk in (the) truth and how to teach/preach\n \n/ Timoteo te enseñará a seguir caminando en (la) verdad y\ncómo enseñar/predicar)\n\nRaya ban kaia lâka yabalka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nroad to everlasting life\n \n/ camino a la vida eterna\n\nYabal saurakku waia\n \n(\nbh10\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto go down a bad road\n \n/ ir por un mal camino\n\nYabalka prakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto block a road\n \n/ bloquear un camino\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmy42\n):\n \nYabalkam prakaia\n \n–\n \nto block your road\n \n/ bloquear tu camino)\n\nYabalka prakanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nroadblock\n \n/ barricada\n\nYabalaya\n \n(a/t:\n \nYabal laya\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nspit\n \n/ saliva\n\nYabalaya tuhbaia\n \n(\nlfb89\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto spit\n \n/ escupir\n\nYaba\n/\nYabba\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nYa ba\n\nYabia\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nYaia\n \n&\n \nYabaia\n\nYahbra\n \n–\n \nnorth\n \n/ norte\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nYa ba yahbra tani kingka sa?\n \n–\n \nWho is (the) king of the north?\n \n/ ¿Quién es (el) rey del norte?\n)\n\nYahbra kati\n \n–\n \nNovember\n \n/ noviembre\n\n(\nLit:\n \nnorth wind moon\n \n/ luna del viento del norte\n)\n\nYahmpus\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nYamhpus\n\nYahpa\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nbig, immense, large, fat, huge\n \n/ grande, inmenso, grande, gordo, enorme\n\nYahpika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nimmensity, largeness, greatness, quantity, size, bulk, magnitude\n \n/ inmensidad, amplitud,\n\ngrandeza, cantidad, tamaño, volumen, magnitud\n\nYahpira\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \ngreat, very big\n \n/ grande, muy grande\n\nB\nî\nla yahpira\n \n(a\n/t:\n \nB\nî\nla yahpa\n,\n \nB\nî\nla tara\n)\n \n–\n \nbig\n-\nmouthed\n \n/\n \ntapudo\n\n(\nNote/\nNota:\n \nused\n \nas an insult /\n \nusado como un insulto)\n\nYahwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make a loud noise, sway (ex: tree)\n \n/ hacer un ruido fuerte, mecer (\nej:\n \nárbol)\n\nIni yahwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nYahwi inaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto cry out loud, to weep, to wail, to lament\n \n/ llorar, llorar a gritos, llorar\ndesaforadamente, gemir, lamentarse\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \ndb-Jems4:9\n:\n \nMan nani sari taks, ini yahwi bas\n \n–\n \nBecome sad, weep\n \n/ Entristezcan, lloren)\n\nYahwanka\n \n–\n \nday after tomorrow\n \n/ pasado mañana\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Luke 13:32\n):\n \nyahwanka tnata alkamna\n \n–\n \nthe day after tomorrow (third day) I will finish\n \n/ pasado mañana (tercero día)\nterminaré)\n\nYaia\n \n(See also the more common synonym / Ver también el sinónimo más común:\n \nYabaia\n) (v-irregular)\n \n–\n \nto give, to\nprovide, to allow, to cause, ...\n \n/ dar, proporcionar, permitir, causar, ...\n\n(Note/Nota: Verb irregularities /\n \nI\nrregularidades\n \ndel verbo\n:\n \nIsna\n \n(\nY\nis\nn\na\n);\n \nIsma\n \n(\nYisma\n);\n \nI\nsa\n \n(\nYisa\n);\n \nYari\n \n(\nYri\n);\n \nYa\nram\n \n(\nY\nram\n);\n \nYama\n\n(\nYma\n);\n \nYabia\n \n(\nYbia\n)\n;\n \nYas\n \n(\nYs\n)\n)\n\nIsa\n \n(v\n-\n3p\n-\npres\n-\nII\n)\n \n–\n \nhe/she gives, he/she allows, he/she causes\n \n/\n \nél/ella da,\n \nél/ella permite, él/ella causa\n\nIsma\n \n(v\n-\n2\np\n-\np\nres\n-\nII\n)\n \n–\n \nyou\n \ng\ni\nve,\n \nyou\n \nallow,\n \nyou\n \ncause\n \n/\n \ntu das, tu permites, tu causa\ns\n\nIsna\n \n(v\n-\n1\np\n-\np\nres\n-\nII\n)\n \n–\n \nI g\ni\nve, I allow, I cause\n \n/ yo\n \ndoy,\n \nyo\n \npermito,\n \nyo\n \ncauso\n\nYabia\n \n(v-3p-fut-II)\n \n–\n \nhe/she will give, he/she will allow, he/she will cause\n \n/ él/ella dará, él/ella permitirá, él/ella\ncausará\n\nYama\n \n(v-2p-fut-II)\n \n–\n \nyou will give, you will allow, you will cause\n \n/ tu daras, tu permitirás, tu causaras\n\nYan\n \n(v-3p-past/pasado)\n \n–\n \ngave, provided, allowed, caused\n \n/ dado, provisto, permitido, causado",
